---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects"
  description="Infrastructure tools and learning projects. Kubernetes operators, eBPF tracers, and distributed systems experiments."
>
  <div class="content-col">
    <div class="rule-label"><span>projects</span></div>

    <ul class="list-none">
      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/k8s-operator" class="proj-name">
            k8s-operator-template
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/k8s-operator" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          A minimal Kubernetes operator scaffolding built with controller-runtime.
          Designed for learning how reconciliation loops work at the control plane level.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">go</span>
          <span class="chip">kubernetes</span>
          <span class="chip">controller-runtime</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/ebpf-tracer" class="proj-name">
            ebpf-tcp-tracer
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/ebpf-tracer" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          TCP connection tracer using eBPF kprobes and perf events.
          Built to understand low-level observability without relying on third-party libraries.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">c</span>
          <span class="chip">ebpf</span>
          <span class="chip">libbpf</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/raft-impl" class="proj-name">
            raft-consensus-go
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/raft-impl" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          Implementation of the Raft consensus algorithm in Go.
          Educational project to understand distributed consensus and leader election mechanics.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">go</span>
          <span class="chip">distributed-systems</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/service-mesh" class="proj-name">
            minimal-service-mesh
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/service-mesh" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          A toy service mesh implementation with Envoy sidecars and a custom control plane.
          Explores xDS protocol and dynamic configuration updates in a real cluster.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">go</span>
          <span class="chip">envoy</span>
          <span class="chip">kubernetes</span>
          <span class="chip">grpc</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/cni-plugin" class="proj-name">
            simple-cni-plugin
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/cni-plugin" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          CNI plugin that sets up network namespaces and veth pairs for container networking.
          Minimal implementation to learn how Kubernetes networking plugins work under the hood.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">go</span>
          <span class="chip">cni</span>
          <span class="chip">networking</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/admission-webhook" class="proj-name">
            k8s-admission-webhook
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/admission-webhook" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          Kubernetes admission webhook that validates and mutates pod specs.
          Used for enforcing security policies and injecting sidecars in a production cluster.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">go</span>
          <span class="chip">kubernetes</span>
          <span class="chip">webhooks</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="proj-item">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline mb-1.5">
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/container-runtime" class="proj-name">
            container-runtime-from-scratch
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/yourname/container-runtime" class="proj-ext">
            ↗ github
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="proj-desc">
          A minimal container runtime built using Linux namespaces, cgroups, and pivot_root.
          Educational implementation to understand what Docker and containerd do at a low level.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
          <span class="chip">c</span>
          <span class="chip">linux</span>
          <span class="chip">containers</span>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
